            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Thanks for taking a look. I agree that combining deferred updates with cursor visibility restoration made this harder to review. I've split the two behaviors:\n\n- This PR now only defers folding-range evaluation and fold updates while editing. It no longer adds C code or tracks cursor visibility across windows.\n- #41773 is a separate dependent draft PR for reopening folds that newly hide a previously visible cursor after a deferred update, including the internal `foldOpenCursor()` binding.\n\nThe mode/snippet transition handling and pending state remain here so the previous evaluated snapshot stays active during editing, including when another operation recomputes folds. Explicit foldclose and client detach handling are also retained. Splitting the behaviors does not eliminate that remaining complexity, but should make it easier to assess separately from the reopening policy.\n\nThe folding-range functional suite passes with 23 tests for this PR and 27 tests with the follow-up applied. The two changes together preserve the original implementation.\n",
